        "After completing over 600 recliner repairs in Greater Noida, our technicians have developed a detailed picture of the fault patterns that are most prevalent in this specific market. The most common call we receive — accounting for roughly 35% of all jobs — is an electric motor that has stopped functioning or is producing a grinding, clicking, or humming noise without completing the reclining cycle. In Greater Noida, this is disproportionately linked to two causes: first, the voltage conversion issues described above, and second, motor burnout caused by power surges during the monsoon season, when Greater Noida's electrical infrastructure — still newer than Delhi's but not without its growing pains — experiences irregular voltage fluctuations. Most homeowners are surprised to learn that a ₹1,800–₹2,500 motor replacement can entirely restore a recliner that appeared completely dead, rather than requiring the ₹40,000–₹80,000 replacement most furniture store staff recommend.",
